1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,510
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,140
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:10,220
But the police
didn't think much of it.

5
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:13,320
They said something like this
couldn't be evidence.

6
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,920
(Joo Ae Sook's Baby (F)
Sept. 11, 2000, 11:05 p.m., 3.28kg)

7
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,700
With Ae Sook at the orphanage.

8
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,510
I met him for the first time
at the interview.

9
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:46,080
It was my dad's
favorite fountain pen.

10
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:56,560
Could I take this
and look at it more closely?

11
00:00:58,030 --> 00:00:59,030
Sure.

12
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:08,310
I was deeply touched by
your interview yesterday, Eun Seol.

13
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,140
When did you prepare
for an interview like that?

14
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:15,880
To win over the directors' votes,
I had no other choice.

15
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,480
Now that I look at it,
you're very brave.

16
00:01:20,290 --> 00:01:22,050
I thought you were just quiet
and hardworking,

17
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:24,920
but I didn't expect you
to do something so bold.

18
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,430
And a live stream on top of that.

19
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:30,260
The Chairman seemed
quite surprised as well.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,960
I didn't tell anyone...

21
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:35,800
because word would get out that
I was using my personal history...

22
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,070
to promote the scholarship program.

23
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,240
Who would think that?

24
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:43,510
Everyone in the company
already knows your story.

25
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,910
People who know all about me
scare me even more.

26
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:51,080
Knowing the truth
doesn't mean they actually get me.

27
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,720
That's true.

28
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,820
Anyway,

29
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:59,920
it seems like you'll be
in the spotlight for a bit.

30
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:04,030
You became a bigger story
than the scholarship program,

31
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,030
as someone who overcame
hardship and adversity.

32
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:09,600
I'm so proud of you.

33
00:02:11,170 --> 00:02:14,210
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

34
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,970
We're not in any danger right now,

35
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:47,140
but we should be prepared
for when we're backed into a corner.

36
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,480
When the investigation closes in,

37
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:53,980
you should wrap things up here...

38
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:56,110
and leave Korea.

39
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,180
Leave Korea?

40
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,990
Manager Na, you're my accomplice.

41
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,390
If you keep holding out here,

42
00:03:05,690 --> 00:03:07,090
you'll end up straight in prison.

43
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:11,000
I don't have a family to support,

44
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:12,960
but your situation is different.

45
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,800
Here.

46
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:23,440
Write a suicide note
containing a confession.

47
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,010
A suicide note?

48
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:31,380
I'll give you 500,000 dollars
for your getaway fund.

49
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,320
Manager Na's suicide note...

50
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:36,220
was written
under Director Joo's coercion.

51
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,520
Of course. No wonder
the handwriting analysis...

52
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:41,590
came back as a match.

53
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,600
Manager Na, you're my accomplice.

54
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:49,630
If you keep holding out here,

55
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,700
you'll end up straight in prison.

56
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:53,810
They're accomplices?

57
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:59,540
Does that mean Director Joo
killed Eun Seol's mother?

58
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,980
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

59
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:12,190
I think we just need to attach
the post-monitoring data.

60
00:04:13,830 --> 00:04:14,830
You're right.

61
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:16,190
For the next board meeting,

62
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:18,930
we can just polish
the existing proposal a bit.

63
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,410
Eun Seol.

64
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:31,110
You really don't say things...

65
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:34,380
you don't mean.

66
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,780
- Excuse me?
- You said it yourself.

67
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,490
You said you had no intention
of hiding your past.

68
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:44,460
Hearing you be so honest
in the interview,

69
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:46,660
I was a little surprised.

70
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:50,660
And it was live, no less.

71
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:52,860
Weren't you nervous at all?

72
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:55,770
Being honest like that
is actually easier for me.

73
00:04:56,730 --> 00:04:59,270
When you try to sugarcoat
or add extra stuff,

74
00:04:59,770 --> 00:05:01,040
that's when it gets tricky.

75
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:04,110
I was just telling it as it is,

76
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:05,640
so I wasn't nervous.

77
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:11,620
I envy you...

78
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:14,190
for being able to be so honest.

79
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:17,220
What's there to envy?

80
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,630
You can be completely honest too,
Secretary Choi.

81
00:05:22,430 --> 00:05:25,360
If you clear your mind
and let go of your greed,

82
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:28,200
then only your true self remains.

83
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:32,040
Then there's nothing
to be intimidated by or afraid of.

84
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:45,620
Seok Jin.

85
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:47,620
How about here?

86
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,660
The vibe here seems a bit better,

87
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:52,360
but it also feels
a little too casual.

88
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:54,230
Which of these places do you prefer?

89
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:55,690
What are these?

90
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,930
What else? Potential venues
for our engagement party.

91
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:01,670
I gave it a lot of thought
and narrowed it down to a few options.

92
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:04,040
Hae Ra.

93
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:06,670
Our engagement...

94
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:08,910
Let's give it a bit more thought.

95
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:12,140
Think about it? What does that mean?

96
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:16,150
I think my mom's having a hard time
accepting our engagement.

97
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:17,220
Ms. Park...

98
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,080
I mean, your mother?

99
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:21,620
Yes.

100
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:25,490
Maybe she thinks she'll lose me
once I'm engaged,

101
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,660
so it's making her anxious.

102
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:28,590
You know how it is.

103
00:06:28,790 --> 00:06:31,000
Whenever my mom gets stressed,
her condition worsens.

104
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:37,570
Does your mom have
separation anxiety from you?

105
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,440
She's throwing a tantrum
like a total child.

106
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,340
Kang Hae Ra.

107
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,680
Fine.

108
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:49,210
But still, postpone the engagement?

109
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:51,920
My dad already gave his permission.

110
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,750
What if we postpone
and he ends up changing his mind?

111
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:56,790
I am not saying
we should postpone it right now.

112
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,960
I just want to buy time
to bring my mom around.

113
00:07:01,090 --> 00:07:02,790
Then should I go
and try to win her over?

114
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,160
There's no point.

115
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:06,830
Seeing you will probably
just make her feel more pressured.

116
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:11,300
How much does she hate me that just
seeing me makes her feel pressured?

117
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,610
Right now, it's not
just about her not liking you.

118
00:07:14,610 --> 00:07:15,610
It's almost as if...

119
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:18,410
she's terrified of something.

120
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:25,350
Ms. Park is driving me crazy.

121
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:29,490
Seok Jin said she isn't on board
with our engagement.

122
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:31,690
What do you mean by that?

123
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:34,990
So Yeon's against your engagement?

124
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,260
Yes.

125
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,930
She's not just against the idea.

126
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,760
Something is making her tremble
with fear.

127
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,500
What?

128
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,600
She's terrified?

129
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,600
That's right.

130
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,570
I mean, does she hate me that much?

131
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:48,970
Or is she that obsessed
with Seok Jin?

132
00:07:49,470 --> 00:07:51,810
I'm about to lose my mind
because of her.

133
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:53,510
Of course.

134
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:56,380
To So Yeon,
Chief Cha is her guardian...

135
00:07:56,450 --> 00:07:58,020
before he's her son.

136
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,480
She's probably terrified
of losing him to you...

137
00:08:00,550 --> 00:08:02,120
once you get engaged.

138
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,920
I said I'd go talk her around,
but he shut that down too.

139
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,020
He said it would just put
too much pressure on her.

140
00:08:07,430 --> 00:08:10,230
Director Joo,
how about you go see her?

141
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:14,070
Since my husband and I
might overwhelm So Yeon,

142
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:18,200
maybe you could go find out
what's on her mind.

143
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,440
Yes, I'll do that.

144
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:30,310
Mr. Seok Jin, you're home.

145
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,780
Hey. What were you up to?

146
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:37,150
This? Auntie put this on for me.

147
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:40,520
I told her I wanted to see
the nice lady.

148
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:43,830
She searched
the nice lady's name online,

149
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,200
and all this popped up.

150
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,770
I've watched this
more than ten times.

151
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,670
Do you like her that much?

152
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:56,970
Of course.

153
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,210
The nice lady is very brave,

154
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,710
and she speaks really well.

155
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:06,080
You're right.
She's really resilient and brave.

156
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:07,820
She's always been like that.

157
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:12,320
I want to eat tteokbokki
with the nice lady...

158
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:14,830
and draw with her too.

159
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,660
Can't I spend time with her?

160
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:24,740
No, seeing her isn't
an option anymore.

161
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,440
From now on,

162
00:09:28,570 --> 00:09:29,810
you'll do those things with Hae Ra.

163
00:09:30,210 --> 00:09:31,580
She's good at drawing too.

164
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:34,650
I don't want to.

165
00:09:36,110 --> 00:09:37,420
I'll go change my clothes.

166
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,680
I want...

167
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:42,250
I want you...

168
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:45,960
to get engaged and even marry...

169
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,760
the nice lady.

170
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:55,830
Why can't it be her?

171
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,840
Welcome...

172
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:04,280
Hello, ma'am.

173
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,740
Where's Eun Guk?

174
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,310
He went on a delivery.

175
00:10:08,850 --> 00:10:10,880
Can I get you
something cold to drink?

176
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:14,120
No need.
Why would I waste money on coffee?

177
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:15,820
I have plenty of coffee at home.

178
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,520
It's on the house,
so have some coffee.

179
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:21,330
Never mind the coffee,
come here and sit down.

180
00:10:29,970 --> 00:10:32,970
Why? Do you have something to say?

181
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:37,010
Why do you keep brushing off
an elder's words like that?

182
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,840
Excuse me?

183
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,340
What do you mean by that?

184
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:41,580
You know what I mean.

185
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:45,480
Why do you keep eyeing Eun Guk?

186
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,790
I haven't been eyeing him.

187
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:51,860
He's just an employee here.

188
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:55,160
Who brings an employee
to their kid's sports day?

189
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:01,170
What if weird rumors start spreading
before he even gets married?

190
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,830
Are you going
to take responsibility?

191
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,340
Wait, no!
You shouldn't take responsibility.

192
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:09,110
Anyway,

193
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:12,810
why do you keep making moves
on my grandson?

194
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,010
I've never made a move on him.

195
00:11:16,450 --> 00:11:18,750
Even if you gave me a truckload
of men like your grandson,

196
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:19,780
I'd refuse.

197
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:22,790
Do you think a single mother
has no taste?

198
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:23,990
I don't want him either.

199
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,290
A grandson raised
by a bitter grandmother...

200
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:27,290
is even worse.

201
00:11:27,530 --> 00:11:29,690
What? Did you call me bitter?

202
00:11:30,490 --> 00:11:34,400
It takes one to know one.
Who's the bitter one here?

203
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:37,300
A woman should be a little gentle.

204
00:11:37,370 --> 00:11:39,670
It's because
you're so harsh and cold...

205
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:42,170
that your kid's father ran off.

206
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:44,040
- Grandmother!
- What the...

207
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:47,240
Watch the cafe for me.

208
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:51,950
Grandmother,
how can you be so cruel?

209
00:11:56,490 --> 00:11:57,560
Right.

210
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:01,460
Raising them with all the love
in the world is useless.

211
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:02,790
What's the point?

212
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:09,900
How much did you lose this time?

213
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,900
That old man, Mr. Kim.

214
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:17,140
His quick hands are no joke.

215
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,880
How about it?

216
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,150
Do you want your son to step in
and get some revenge for you?

217
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:23,780
Like that.

218
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:29,490
This is all because
you're so useless.

219
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:30,790
What?

220
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:33,190
You losing money playing cards
is my fault?

221
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:38,160
My precious eldest grandson
is dating a single mother.

222
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,730
As his father,
aren't you concerned at all?

223
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:42,830
Is that what this is about?

224
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,940
But Eun Guk denied it.

225
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,640
He said their relationship
is strictly professional.

226
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:51,040
And you believe that?

227
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,880
What are you hitting me for?

228
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,710
Look at Eun Guk's eyes.

229
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:58,220
Every time he looks at her,

230
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:01,350
he gets this dreamy look in his eyes
and grins like a fool.

231
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:04,320
And don't even get me started
on her.

232
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:08,530
She acts like she's ready
to give him the world.

233
00:13:11,030 --> 00:13:12,860
Are they really dating?

234
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,930
It makes my blood boil.

235
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:16,900
I can't believe it.

236
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:23,470
I heard your mother
is against your engagement.

237
00:13:23,570 --> 00:13:24,640
Is that true?

238
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:25,940
Yes.

239
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:29,480
I think she's afraid of losing me
after I get engaged.

240
00:13:30,650 --> 00:13:32,080
That makes sense.

241
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:36,220
Getting engaged means
marriage isn't far off.

242
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,260
My mother's sensitive to changes
in her surroundings.

243
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:42,930
We need to give her time...

244
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:45,130
so she can slowly adjust
to everything.

245
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:46,730
Right.

246
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:49,670
If that's how she feels,
we should wait for her.

247
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:55,210
The CEO prepared a gift
for your mother.

248
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:59,310
If you don't mind,
could I hand it to her myself?

249
00:14:01,010 --> 00:14:02,010
Personally?

250
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:03,450
Yes.

251
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:07,920
I'll go instead, as the CEO and
the Chairman might intimidate her.

252
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:12,220
Besides, it'd be good for me
to build a relationship with her.

253
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:14,530
It'll make it easier for her
to adjust later.

254
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:18,200
That'd be great, thank you.

255
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:21,470
Good, then I'll go see her
on my own today.

256
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,840
- Hello.
- Hello.

257
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:28,540
Hello.

258
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:43,290
Why do those two...

259
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,990
keep hanging around each other?

260
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:51,000
Find out what Ko Eun Seol
and Seo Hyun Jae are up to.

261
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:54,370
I've noticed them spending
a lot of time together lately.

262
00:14:55,670 --> 00:14:57,970
It doesn't seem like Ko Eun Seol...

263
00:14:57,970 --> 00:15:00,200
is up to anything
in particular right now.

264
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,870
She's monitoring public reaction
to the interview,

265
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:05,680
on top of preparing
for the upcoming board meeting.

266
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,310
Do you think I don't know that?

267
00:15:09,650 --> 00:15:11,050
Are you really going to sit back...

268
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:13,350
and get blindsided again
like her last interview?

269
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:15,090
Didn't I tell you?

270
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,990
If we drop our guard for a second,

271
00:15:16,990 --> 00:15:18,720
who knows what she might pull next.

272
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,260
Yes, understood.

273
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:23,930
Ms. Joo, did you know?

274
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:26,730
I think Secretary Choi
and Ko Eun Seol are dating.

275
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:30,300
Who said they are dating?

276
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,170
The other day, I saw them
drinking together at a bar.

277
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,470
Totally busted.

278
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:40,180
Track Seo Hyun Jae's movements
and report back.

279
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:43,110
- Sure.
- You may go.

280
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:46,820
Secretary Choi.

281
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,360
Don't get drunk on cheap sympathy.

282
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:55,530
We don't have time
to play around with emotions.

283
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:58,160
Is that clear?

284
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,800
Yes, I'll keep that in mind.

285
00:16:14,350 --> 00:16:16,950
Your strategy worked
after all, Eun Seol.

286
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:19,120
I mean,
the scholarship project aside,

287
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,550
a reaction like this...

288
00:16:20,550 --> 00:16:23,090
should work out great
for the retrial.

289
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:25,060
I know.

290
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:26,960
I think doing the interview
was a good idea.

291
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,190
See?

292
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:30,730
I told you
that you were made for the stage.

293
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,600
You're keeping your distance
from Director Joo, right?

294
00:16:41,810 --> 00:16:42,810
Yes.

295
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:44,980
Even without trying
to distance myself,

296
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,780
I just don't feel
as comfortable around her anymore.

297
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:48,910
Whenever I'm around her,

298
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:53,080
I can't help feeling tense
and uneasy.

299
00:16:55,290 --> 00:16:56,890
I'm telling you this just in case,

300
00:16:57,390 --> 00:17:00,290
but if she approaches you first,

301
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:03,530
be on your guard. Okay?

302
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,760
Sure.

303
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:11,170
But why are you so wary
of Director Joo?

304
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Well...

305
00:17:16,110 --> 00:17:17,880
I'll tell you everything
when the time comes.

306
00:17:18,810 --> 00:17:20,640
What is it? I'm dying to know.

307
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,780
Can't you just tell me now?

308
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:28,020
Gosh, I'm hungry.

309
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,550
What should we eat today?

310
00:17:30,350 --> 00:17:31,490
What should we get?

311
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:35,830
Hello.

312
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:38,460
Hi. Have you been well, So Yeon?

313
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,100
Yes.

314
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:42,170
Wait.

315
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:44,500
Are you here all by yourself?

316
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,500
Today's Auntie's day off.

317
00:17:48,710 --> 00:17:50,210
I see.

318
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:52,740
Please have a seat.

319
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,610
Right, thank you.

320
00:17:57,110 --> 00:18:00,020
You draw very well, So Yeon.

321
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:05,090
Yes. I like drawing.

322
00:18:08,390 --> 00:18:09,490
So Yeon,

323
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,700
I have a quick question for you.

324
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,800
Do you mind if I ask?

325
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:17,940
Not at all, go ahead.

326
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:22,770
Chief Cha's father
and CEO Kang Young Hoon.

327
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,180
They must've been really close.

328
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:29,750
No, they weren't close at all.

329
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,020
Just because they're friends
doesn't mean they're actually close.

330
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,650
Yes, of course.

331
00:18:35,850 --> 00:18:37,320
That's certainly possible.

332
00:18:38,890 --> 00:18:40,420
They fought often.

333
00:18:41,230 --> 00:18:44,960
So my husband was very, very upset.

334
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:48,530
I see.

335
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:51,640
Then, So Yeon,

336
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:55,470
do you remember
what happened on the day...

337
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:58,210
Chief Cha's father had his accident?

338
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,150
No.

339
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:09,420
Not really. I don't know.
I don't remember.

340
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,960
That's okay. It's fine.

341
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:16,660
Well, if anything comes back to you,

342
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,760
could you tell me?

343
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:22,270
Yes.

344
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:27,170
Thank you, So Yeon.

345
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:31,580
So, you met with So Yeon?

346
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:33,580
Yes.

347
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:36,480
I also handed over
the gift we prepared.

348
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:38,020
Good.

349
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:41,890
Did you manage to learn anything
about So Yeon's condition?

350
00:19:42,590 --> 00:19:44,190
Knowing she was traumatized...

351
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:45,760
by what happened
with Chief Cha's father,

352
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:48,930
I brought it up very carefully.

353
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,460
Did you?

354
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,530
Did she seem to know anything?

355
00:19:55,170 --> 00:19:58,640
No. It seems like she can't
remember anything right now.

356
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:02,140
Right, those memories
wouldn't return so easily.

357
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:05,140
Still,

358
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,780
she told me a lot of things.

359
00:20:10,010 --> 00:20:11,480
What kind of things?

360
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:15,150
About what kind of person
Chief Cha's father was,

361
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:17,690
I was able to hear in detail.

362
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:20,760
Is that so?

363
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:23,930
Yes. If we keep talking,

364
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:27,560
I might be able to find out
what brought on the shock...

365
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,270
on the day of the accident.

366
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:33,670
Even so, there's no need
to push and provoke a sick person.

367
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,340
I heard So Yeon...

368
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:38,680
needs stability
in her life right now.

369
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:42,080
I'll be careful
so you don't have to worry.

370
00:20:43,250 --> 00:20:44,250
Good.

371
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:45,450
Also,

372
00:20:46,450 --> 00:20:49,350
report everything to me
regarding So Yeon,

373
00:20:49,990 --> 00:20:52,220
no matter how small,
and don't leave anything out.

374
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,060
Yes, I'll do that.

375
00:21:08,210 --> 00:21:11,110
I need to change
Ms. Park's mind somehow.

376
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:15,350
How can I get her on board?

377
00:21:18,050 --> 00:21:19,150
Ko Eun Seol...

378
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:22,020
probably knows how to win her over.

379
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:26,620
Ko Eun Seol.

380
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:37,970
What did you do
with Seok Jin's mom last time?

381
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:40,370
Excuse me?

382
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:43,570
What did you two do while
you were at the cafe last time?

383
00:21:44,070 --> 00:21:47,010
I mean, I saw some coloring books.

384
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,850
Don't tell me you did something
that childish.

385
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:50,810
It wasn't childish at all.

386
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,920
We enjoyed
a therapeutic activity together.

387
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:54,320
Therapeutic, my foot.

388
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:57,390
So, which coloring book was it?

389
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:16,440
She might struggle a bit at first,
but she picks things up fast.

390
00:22:16,670 --> 00:22:18,180
She's also able to stay focused
for a long time.

391
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:20,680
Hold on. Why is this so complicated?

392
00:22:22,150 --> 00:22:23,550
That woman actually does this?

393
00:22:23,710 --> 00:22:27,350
If you just guide her well at first,
she'll catch on quickly.

394
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,190
Whatever. You're dismissed.

395
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,330
This is ridiculously complicated.

396
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:43,400
What? Stop!

397
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:46,640
That's not how you do it.

398
00:22:47,170 --> 00:22:49,010
- Seriously.
- I know.

399
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:50,940
It's just not going very well.

400
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:52,540
Like this. Watch.

401
00:22:52,610 --> 00:22:55,680
You have to do it gently like this.

402
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,950
You were being so rough...

403
00:22:57,950 --> 00:23:00,020
that you ended up coloring
outside the lines.

404
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:03,150
- Now what?
- I get it, so please be quiet.

405
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:07,160
The nice lady...

406
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:09,190
is really good at this.

407
00:23:09,190 --> 00:23:12,000
It's always Ko Eun Seol with you!

408
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:14,030
Stop comparing me to her.

409
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:16,200
Why do you keep asking for her
when I'm treating you so well?

410
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:20,300
Okay. Look, I'm sorry.

411
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,940
Don't be mad, Hae Ra.

412
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,210
This is so annoying.

413
00:23:24,710 --> 00:23:27,310
I'm trying to be nice,
but you're not helping.

414
00:23:27,310 --> 00:23:30,810
Ms. Park, learn to read the room,
will you?

415
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:34,620
Okay. I said I'm sorry.

416
00:23:35,050 --> 00:23:39,220
Look, Hae Ra.
Let's try doing this one more time.

417
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:41,530
I said I really don't want to.

418
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,230
Mom.

419
00:23:46,530 --> 00:23:47,760
Seok Jin, you're home.

420
00:23:48,300 --> 00:23:49,470
Were you drawing?

421
00:23:49,630 --> 00:23:52,600
Yes. Mother and I were
having fun coloring.

422
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,210
Right, Mother?

423
00:23:56,610 --> 00:23:57,710
Nicely done.

424
00:23:59,340 --> 00:24:00,610
Mom, where are you going?

425
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:03,080
I'm tired.

426
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:07,180
She's probably exhausted
after daycare today.

427
00:24:07,620 --> 00:24:08,950
You'll give me a ride home,
won't you?

428
00:24:09,690 --> 00:24:10,750
Sure, let's go.

429
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:27,400
- I'm home.
- Hey.

430
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:31,270
- Where's Grandma?
- She went to the senior center.

431
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:34,510
- I'll go wash up.
- Hey, come here for a second.

432
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,390
Your grandma told me...

433
00:24:42,790 --> 00:24:44,550
that you're dating Teun Teun's Mom.

434
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:48,090
Is there really something
going on between you two?

435
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:49,560
No.

436
00:24:50,090 --> 00:24:52,360
Grandma just got
the wrong idea about things.

437
00:24:53,330 --> 00:24:54,900
I wouldn't say she's totally off.

438
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:57,500
I've been sensing it
for a while, too.

439
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:01,300
Hey, do you really not have feelings
for Teun Teun's mom?

440
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:05,080
Honestly, I don't know.

441
00:25:05,610 --> 00:25:07,410
I can't tell
if I actually like her...

442
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:09,780
or if it's simply
because she's so nice.

443
00:25:10,610 --> 00:25:12,850
So, break it down for me.

444
00:25:13,150 --> 00:25:14,920
How do you feel about her, exactly?

445
00:25:17,150 --> 00:25:18,590
Well, I like seeing the boss.

446
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:21,160
I like how her eyes look
a bit puffy in the morning,

447
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:24,760
and it's adorable when she snaps
and raises her voice.

448
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:29,070
Especially when she gets all red
for no reason...

449
00:25:29,330 --> 00:25:31,330
and reacts to every little thing
when I tease her.

450
00:25:33,170 --> 00:25:34,270
She's so cute.

451
00:25:34,940 --> 00:25:37,270
You've already fallen for her.

452
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:40,540
Man, your grandma was right.

453
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:43,310
You're totally
head over heels for her.

454
00:25:44,180 --> 00:25:45,180
But...

455
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,220
if you aren't going
to take it seriously,

456
00:25:48,290 --> 00:25:49,390
don't even bother starting.

457
00:25:51,190 --> 00:25:52,590
Dad, didn't you say...

458
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:55,060
you'd support me no matter what
if I liked her?

459
00:25:56,030 --> 00:25:59,830
That's only if you're truly serious
and willing to go all the way.

460
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,560
If you change your mind
halfway through,

461
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:03,330
you can just back out.

462
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:05,570
But what about Teun Teun's Mom
and Teun Teun?

463
00:26:06,540 --> 00:26:08,710
So think about this very carefully.

464
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:33,700
- Hey.
- Are you busy?

465
00:26:34,330 --> 00:26:36,130
No, is something up?

466
00:26:36,570 --> 00:26:37,770
Nothing in particular.

467
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,800
How about a beer?

468
00:26:39,940 --> 00:26:41,140
Sure. Sounds good.

469
00:26:41,970 --> 00:26:42,970
Here.

470
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:54,280
Why? Is something on your mind?

471
00:26:54,580 --> 00:26:56,790
No, not really.

472
00:27:00,190 --> 00:27:02,860
What is it? Tell me right now.

473
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:04,730
I'm your Genie, remember?

474
00:27:04,930 --> 00:27:07,160
The one who grants all your wishes.

475
00:27:10,170 --> 00:27:13,540
I just feel a little frustrated,
that's all.

476
00:27:15,810 --> 00:27:16,810
What's going on?

477
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:22,280
Actually, I saw Teun Teun's dad
at the cafe recently.

478
00:27:22,550 --> 00:27:24,650
What? That jerk?

479
00:27:25,320 --> 00:27:26,480
What did you say?

480
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,850
He was with his girlfriend.

481
00:27:29,420 --> 00:27:31,120
They just happened to drop by.

482
00:27:31,250 --> 00:27:32,760
He didn't know it was my cafe.

483
00:27:33,690 --> 00:27:36,890
He did try to contact me after that,
but I ignored him.

484
00:27:39,100 --> 00:27:40,100
Good.

485
00:27:41,130 --> 00:27:42,970
If he ever contacts you again,
tell me.

486
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,300
I'll take care of it.

487
00:27:44,630 --> 00:27:47,070
As if you can actually do anything.

488
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:49,810
He won't be calling again. Here.

489
00:27:53,710 --> 00:27:54,710
Right.

490
00:27:55,180 --> 00:27:57,880
You should forget about that jerk
and start fresh.

491
00:27:58,550 --> 00:28:00,720
You're crazy. Start fresh, my foot.

492
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:03,020
If you can't do it,
I'll make the move for you.

493
00:28:03,350 --> 00:28:06,420
I'll definitely make sure
Eun Seol's grandmother likes me.

494
00:28:06,690 --> 00:28:08,890
Then she won't be able to say
she dislikes you.

495
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:11,730
Seo Hyun Jae, it's not like that.

496
00:28:12,230 --> 00:28:16,430
Also, square your shoulders
like this.

497
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:19,200
Come on. What are you worried about?

498
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:22,540
You've got a reliable lawyer
for a brother right by your side.

499
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:25,480
So don't be intimidated.

500
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:27,880
I'll take care of everything.

501
00:28:29,450 --> 00:28:30,880
Here. Cheers.

502
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:34,020
I'm Genie, so tell me your wish.

503
00:28:35,790 --> 00:28:38,690
I met with the board members
for lunch today.

504
00:28:39,620 --> 00:28:40,960
The foundation directors?

505
00:28:41,460 --> 00:28:43,530
Yes, and while we ate,

506
00:28:43,730 --> 00:28:47,200
I asked them to look favorably
on your scholarship program.

507
00:28:48,770 --> 00:28:50,070
Why would you do that?

508
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:54,340
Even if you didn't say anything,

509
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:57,310
it would've passed
at the next board meeting.

510
00:28:57,810 --> 00:28:59,240
Still, as the CEO,

511
00:28:59,510 --> 00:29:02,050
wouldn't it help
if I put in a good word?

512
00:29:02,350 --> 00:29:05,650
Ever since Eun Seol's interview,
public opinion has improved,

513
00:29:05,880 --> 00:29:09,050
so the board won't oppose it much.

514
00:29:09,450 --> 00:29:12,620
If you step in,
it'll just overshadow...

515
00:29:12,890 --> 00:29:14,560
all of Eun Seol's hard work.

516
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:17,990
So you're saying...

517
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:20,060
I shouldn't have gotten involved?

518
00:29:20,900 --> 00:29:21,900
Is that it?

519
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:24,100
Why take it like that?

520
00:29:24,670 --> 00:29:25,700
Fine,

521
00:29:26,300 --> 00:29:27,370
thanks for trying.

522
00:29:34,540 --> 00:29:36,450
(Cheongma)

523
00:29:36,610 --> 00:29:39,750
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

524
00:29:40,380 --> 00:29:42,320
Even if I don't say anything
to Eun Seol,

525
00:29:43,450 --> 00:29:45,690
I should give Director Joo
a warning in advance.

526
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:56,270
Hello, Director Joo.

527
00:29:56,870 --> 00:29:58,670
This is Seo Hyun Jae
from the Legal Team.

528
00:29:59,070 --> 00:30:00,200
Right, Mr. Seo.

529
00:30:01,070 --> 00:30:02,810
This is a surprise.

530
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:08,850
Sure, where should we meet?

531
00:30:10,980 --> 00:30:12,750
Got it. I'll see you there.

532
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:17,250
Was that Team Leader Seo?

533
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:18,690
Yes.

534
00:30:19,890 --> 00:30:23,130
I have no clue
why he's suddenly acting like this.

535
00:30:24,090 --> 00:30:26,460
Should I go with you, just in case?

536
00:30:27,230 --> 00:30:28,230
No.

537
00:30:28,430 --> 00:30:29,870
If you come with me,

538
00:30:29,870 --> 00:30:31,500
it might actually look
even stranger.

539
00:30:32,300 --> 00:30:33,670
I'll meet him alone today.

540
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:37,010
Understood. I'll wait at the office.

541
00:30:42,550 --> 00:30:45,450
For you to request
a private meeting like this...

542
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:47,980
I'm curious what this is about.

543
00:30:49,890 --> 00:30:51,990
I prepared a small gift
for you as well.

544
00:30:53,390 --> 00:30:54,390
A gift?

545
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:57,030
You turned down mine,

546
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:59,600
but you got me a gift?

547
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:04,470
Yes, it's a gift
I absolutely have to give you.

548
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:09,340
I wonder what that gift could be.

549
00:31:10,870 --> 00:31:13,180
Strictly speaking,
I'm not the one who prepared it.

550
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:17,710
Manager Na Tae Hoon...

551
00:31:18,450 --> 00:31:20,550
left this gift for you.

552
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:25,920
Manager Na?

553
00:31:51,910 --> 00:31:53,550
(Joo Ae Sook's Baby (F)
Sept. 11, 2000, 11:05 p.m., 3.28kg)

554
00:32:03,230 --> 00:32:06,200
In case seeing these gifts...

555
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:08,530
makes you miss
Manager Na Tae Hoon too badly,

556
00:32:10,370 --> 00:32:12,700
I also brought along
a recorded message from him.

557
00:32:14,170 --> 00:32:15,610
We're not in any danger right now,

558
00:32:16,470 --> 00:32:19,810
but we should be prepared
for when we're backed into a corner.

559
00:32:22,210 --> 00:32:23,880
When the investigation closes in,

560
00:32:24,950 --> 00:32:26,480
you should wrap things up here...

561
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:28,450
and leave Korea.

562
00:33:01,850 --> 00:33:05,690
(A Trap Called Desire)

563
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:08,090
Director Joo will approach
Eun Seol first.

564
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:10,830
I've got to tell Eun Seol the truth
about who Ms. Joo really is first.

565
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:13,100
Since you have
a great sense of style,

566
00:33:13,130 --> 00:33:14,400
could you help me plan
my engagement party?

567
00:33:14,460 --> 00:33:16,830
Ko Eun Seol, even if you're new
to the corporate world,

568
00:33:16,900 --> 00:33:17,970
shouldn't you at least know
the difference here?

569
00:33:18,030 --> 00:33:19,540
You have to show them with results.

570
00:33:19,670 --> 00:33:21,800
Imprint on their minds
that you're the one...

571
00:33:21,870 --> 00:33:23,370
meant to lead Cheongma.

572
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:25,410
Send some guys over there
and just scare them a little.

573
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,940
I heard he has an older sister
and a nephew.

574
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:29,780
Well, what can you do about it?

575
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,680
Manager Na made all of this up.

576
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:33,980
Since you've been digging
into my background,

577
00:33:34,020 --> 00:33:36,490
you must know what Eun Seol and I
are to each other.

578
00:33:38,220 --> 00:33:40,190
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
